Handle the per-screen lifecycle of Xnest host cursors.

The root cursor is created before input devices are initialized. Device
startup realizes it only on the initial screen, but FreeCursor() calls
UnrealizeCursor for every screen. With multiple screens, resetting Xnest
therefore dereferences a NULL cursor private. Displaying the root cursor
on another screen can fail the same way in xnestSetCursor().

Realize cursors on demand when displaying them, reuse existing host
cursors, and allow cleanup and recoloring before realization. Clear the
private pointer when freeing a host cursor. The reset crash also occurs
in vanilla xorg-server 21.1.24.

Upstream report:
https://github.com/XQuartz/XQuartz/issues/518

--- a/hw/xnest/Cursor.c
+++ b/hw/xnest/Cursor.c
@@ -41,11 +41,19 @@
